.TH SDL_GetAudioRecordingDevices 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetAudioRecordingDevices \- Get a list of currently-connected audio recording devices.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_AudioDeviceID * SDL_GetAudioRecordingDevices(int *count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This returns of list of available devices that record audio, like a microphone (\(dqrecording\(dq devices)\[char46] If you want devices that play sound, perhaps to speakers or headphones (\(dqplayback\(dq devices), use
.BR SDL_GetAudioPlaybackDevices ()
instead\[char46]
.PP
This only returns a list of physical devices; it will not have any device IDs returned by
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDevice ()\[char46]
.PP
If this function returns NULL, to signify an error,
.BR *count
will be set to zero\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I count
a pointer filled in with the number of devices returned, may be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a 0 terminated array of device instance IDs, or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46] This should be freed with
.BR SDL_free ()
when it is no longer needed\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDevice (3),
.BR SDL_GetAudioPlaybackDevices (3)
